# Executive offsites now live in the /offsite/ folder of this repo and are served directly.
# The old proxy to offsite.kuma.partners has been removed on purpose.
# Do not add a rule redirecting /offsite to /offsite/: Netlify treats both as the same
# path, so such a rule redirects to itself and causes ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS.

# Standalone offsite configurator for outbound links. Netlify already serves
# configurator.html for /offsite/configurator; this 200 rewrite also covers the
# trailing-slash form (Netlify matches rules with or without the slash). It is a
# rewrite to a file, never a redirect, so it cannot loop.
/offsite/configurator   /offsite/configurator.html   200

# Offsite pages. The new design sits at the top level of the repo (offsite-v2.html with
# offsite-v2.css and offsite-v2.js, and offsite-partners-v2.html with offsite-partners-v2.css
# and offsite-partners-v2.js). Forced 200 rewrites show them at /offsite/ and
# /offsite/partners.html (internal, the address stays the same). The old files
# (new.html, offsite/index.html, offsite/partners.html) stay in the repo for now and are not served.
# The old draft address /offsite/new sends people to /offsite/ for good.
# To go back to the previous design: point the /offsite/ rules at /new.html and delete the two
# partners rules, so /offsite/partners.html serves its own file again.
/offsite/new                /offsite/                    301!
/offsite/new.html           /offsite/                    301!
/offsite/                   /offsite-v2.html             200!
/offsite/index.html         /offsite-v2.html             200!
/offsite/partners           /offsite-partners-v2.html    200!
/offsite/partners.html      /offsite-partners-v2.html    200!

# The Round lives at /round/ (moved 28 Oct 2026 from theround.kuma.partners, then from /the-round/
# on 30 Oct 2026). The old addresses and the convenience alias 301 to the new page. Deep paths under the old folders also land on /round/, because the old subpages no longer exist. Do not add a
# rule from /round to /round/: Netlify treats both as the same path, so it would redirect to itself.
/the-round     /round/          301!
/the-round/*   /round/          301!
/theround      /round/          301!
/theround/*    /round/          301!
